From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zerogap <zerogap@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:19:29 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] QRDetector: no alignment pattern search far outside the image

SampleQR estimates the bottom right alignment pattern where two pairs of
lines meet. For (almost) parallel lines that point is huge, infinite or
NaN, and LocateAlignmentPattern converted it to int (in a log line that
is evaluated even without PRINT_DEBUG): undefined behaviour, found by
fuzzing with UBSan (-fsanitize=float-cast-overflow).

None of the points LocateAlignmentPattern looks at (within 2.8 module
sizes of the estimate) is in the image then, so return early: same
results.
---
 core/src/qrcode/QRDetector.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/src/qrcode/QRDetector.cpp b/core/src/qrcode/QRDetector.cpp
index f96a8620..9b4cdbfd 100644
--- a/core/src/qrcode/QRDetector.cpp
+++ b/core/src/qrcode/QRDetector.cpp
@@ -402,6 +402,10 @@ static PerspectiveTransform Mod2Pix(int dimension, PointF brOffset, Quadrilatera
 
 static std::optional<PointF> LocateAlignmentPattern(const BitMatrix& image, double moduleSize, PointF estimate)
 {
+	// an estimate far outside the image (where almost parallel lines meet, or NaN): none of the points below is in it
+	if (!image.isIn(estimate, -int(std::ceil(3 * moduleSize))))
+		return {};
+
 	log(estimate, LOG_R);
 	log_l("LocateAlignmentPattern: local modSize = %.3f @ (%d, %d)", moduleSize, PointI(estimate).x * 5 + 2, PointI(estimate).y * 5 + 2);
 
